<report>
<title>Sign test</title>

<p><b>For @sample observations with @sample_1 on one side:</b></p>

<block name="exact">
<p>Cumulative probability<br />
<pval>Two sided @{prob_2:pval}</pval><br />
<pval>One sided @{prob_1:pval}</pval></p>
</block>
<block name="large"><p><warn>sample is too large for an exact calculation</warn></p></block>

<p>Normal approximate z = @{z:roundu}<br />
<pval>Two sided @{p_2:pval}</pval><br />
<pval>One sided @{p_1:pval}</pval></p>

<p><b><ci>Exact (Clopper-Pearson) @ci% confidence interval for the proportion:</ci></b></p>
<table>
<tr><td><ci>Lower Limit =</ci></td><td><ci>@{lower:roundu}</ci></td></tr>
<tr><td><ci>Proportion =</ci></td><td><ci>@{prop:roundu}</ci></td></tr>
<tr><td><ci>Upper Limit =</ci></td><td><ci>@upper</ci></td></tr>
</table>
</report>
